B.aQk=new A.O("Smith (2019) says that pollution is bad.","Smith (2019) argues that industrial pollution is a primary driver of respiratory illness.","say akademik at\u0131fta tav\u0131r bildirmeyen zay\u0131f bir fiildir; kayna\u011f\u0131n ne yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131na g\xf6re argue, note, demonstrate ya da claim se\xe7ilir ve iddia belirsiz s\u0131fatlarla de\u011fil kesin ifadeyle aktar\u0131l\u0131r.",null)
B.aMa=new A.O("The results were be analysed with SPSS.","The results were analysed with SPSS.","Edilgen be fiili + \xfc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc h\xe2l ile kurulur ve be yaln\u0131zca bir kez gelir: were zaten be fiilinin ge\xe7mi\u015f bi\xe7imidir, ard\u0131ndan ikinci bir be gelemez.",null)
B.aMI=new A.O("He said me that the data was wrong.","He told me that the data were incorrect.","say ki\u015fiyi do\u011frudan nesne almaz (say to me), tell al\u0131r; ayr\u0131ca akademik kay\u0131tta data \xe7o\u011ful kabul edilir ve wrong yerine incorrect ya da inconsistent tercih edilir.",null)
B.bA4=s([B.aJp,B.aQk,B.aMa,B.aMI],t.Z)
B.c6O=new A.bw("a-06-formal-grammar","Edilgen yap\u0131, aktarma ve at\u0131f fiilleri: kayna\u011f\u0131 do\u011fru konu\u015fturmak","Bu ad\u0131mda akademik yaz\u0131n\u0131n iki zorunlu yap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorsun: edilgen \xe7at\u0131 (passive) ve dolayl\u0131 aktarma (reported speech), art\u0131 bu ikisini birle\u015ftiren at\u0131f fiilleri. Edilgen, y\xf6ntem b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcnde failin de\u011fil i\u015flemin \xf6nemli oldu\u011fu yerlerde standartt\u0131r; aktarma ise literat\xfcrdeki her c\xfcmlenin temelidir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc akademik metin b\xfcy\xfck \xf6l\xe7\xfcde ba\u015fkalar\u0131n\u0131n iddialar\u0131n\u0131 aktar\u0131p de\u011ferlendirmekten olu\u015fur. At\u0131f fiili se\xe7imi teknik bir ayr\u0131nt\u0131 de\u011fil, tav\u0131r bildirimidir: Smith argues, Smith claims ve Smith demonstrates c\xfcmleleri ayn\u0131 kayna\u011fa kar\u015f\u0131 \xfc\xe7 farkl\u0131 mesafe kurar; bu ad\u0131mda o mesafeyi bilin\xe7li se\xe7meyi \xf6\u011freneceksin.",B.bpL,B.bbG,B.bA4,"Kal\u0131plar drillinde passive setini a\xe7 ve yirmi be\u015f soruyu seksen sekiz puan \xfcst\xfcnde bitir; her sorudan \xf6nce be fiilinin hangi zamanda oldu\u011funu sesli s\xf6yle, her yanl\u0131\u015fta c\xfcmleyi bir kez etken kurup hangisinin daha do\u011fal durdu\u011funu kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131r. Ard\u0131ndan kendi alan\u0131ndan okudu\u011fun son makaleden \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmle se\xe7 ve her birini d\xf6rt kez aktar: bir kez argues, bir kez claims, bir kez demonstrates, bir kez notes ile; her aktarmada kayna\u011fa kurdu\u011fun mesafenin nas\u0131l de\u011fi\u015fti\u011fini tek c\xfcmleyle yaz ve son olarak ayn\u0131 \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmleyi It has been argued that \u2026 kal\u0131b\u0131yla parantez i\xe7i at\u0131f ekleyerek yeniden kur.",B.j,null,null,null,null)
B.b1r=new A.r("Ara\u015ft\u0131rman\u0131n iskelet kelimeleri","Bir ara\u015ft\u0131rma metnini ta\u015f\u0131yan kelimeler s\u0131n\u0131rl\u0131d\u0131r ve hepsi \xe7ift h\xe2linde \xf6\u011frenilir: hypothesis (\xe7o\u011fulu hypotheses) ve onu test etmek (test a hypothesis), sample ve sample size (\xf6rneklem \xe7ekmek: draw a sample), participants, variable (independent ve dependent), measure ve instrument. methodology ile method fark\u0131 s\u0131nav kadar tezde de sorulur: method tek tek uygulanan i\u015flemdir (a questionnaire, a semi-structured interview), methodology ise bu y\xf6ntemlerin se\xe7imini gerek\xe7elendiren \xe7er\xe7evedir. Sonu\xe7 b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcn\xfcn kelimeleri de sabittir: findings, correlation, association, effect size, statistically significant, reliability (tutarl\u0131l\u0131k) ve validity (\xf6l\xe7t\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc \xf6l\xe7me). Bu son iki kelimeyi kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rmak okura y\xf6ntem bilgisizli\u011fi olarak g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr. K\u0131s\u0131t bildiren kelimeler akademik d\xfcr\xfcstl\xfc\u011f\xfcn par\xe7as\u0131d\u0131r: limitation, constraint, scope, generalisability, confounding variable, self-report bias. \u0130yi bir tez bunlar\u0131 gizlemez, kendi b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcnde toplar. Her kelimeyi ailesiyle \xf6\u011fren: analyse / analysis / analytical, significant / significance / significantly, reliable / reliability, hypothesise / hypothesis / hypothetical; \xe7\xfcnk\xfc akademik yaz\u0131da ayn\u0131 k\xf6k\xfc farkl\u0131 s\xf6zc\xfck t\xfcr\xfcnde kullanman gerekir.")
B.aT1=new A.r("Literat\xfcr taramas\u0131 dili: ne biliniyor, ne eksik","Literat\xfcr taramas\u0131 \xfc\xe7 hareketten olu\u015fur ve her hareketin kendi kal\u0131b\u0131 vard\u0131r: alan\u0131 \xf6zetlemek, bo\u015flu\u011fu g\xf6stermek, kendi \xe7al\u0131\u015fman\u0131 o bo\u015flu\u011fa yerle\u015ftirmek. Alan\u0131 \xf6zetlemek i\xe7in present perfect kullan\u0131l\u0131r \xe7\xfcnk\xfc birikmi\u015f bir bilgi g\xf6vdesinden s\xf6z edersin: Previous studies have shown that feedback improves accuracy; There is a growing body of literature on academic procrastination. Tek bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fmadan s\xf6z ederken ge\xe7mi\u015f zamana ge\xe7ilir: Kaya (2021) found that the effect disappeared after one year. Bu iki zaman aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015f, iyi yaz\u0131lm\u0131\u015f bir taraman\u0131n en belirgin i\u015faretidir. Bo\u015fluk c\xfcmlesi taraman\u0131n can al\u0131c\u0131 noktas\u0131d\u0131r ve nazik bir olumsuzlamayla kurulur: However, little attention has been paid to its timing; To date, few studies have examined this effect in bilingual learners. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc hareket kendi katk\u0131n\u0131 ba\u011flar: The present study addresses this gap by comparing two feedback schedules. Bu c\xfcmle olmadan tarama, kaynak listesi gibi okunur ve ara\u015ft\u0131rma sorunun neden \xf6nemli oldu\u011fu belirsiz kal\u0131r.")
B.aTV=new A.r("Tehlikeli kelimeler: significant, prove, correlate, control","significant akademik metinde g\xfcnl\xfck anlam\u0131n\u0131 kaybeder: istatistiksel anlaml\u0131l\u0131k demektir. B\xfcy\xfckl\xfck anlatmak istiyorsan substantial, considerable, marked kullan; very significant ifadesinden ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131l\u0131r, highly significant ise ancak p de\u011feriyle birlikte (p < .001 gibi) kullan\u0131l\u0131r. prove matematik ve mant\u0131k d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda neredeyse hi\xe7 kullan\u0131lmaz; bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fma sonucu i\xe7in support, indicate, provide evidence for do\u011fru fiillerdir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc tek bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fma bir iddiay\u0131 kan\u0131tlamaz. correlate edat\u0131n\u0131 sabit al\u0131r: correlate with, correlation between A and B; ve korelasyon nedensellik de\u011fildir. Bulguyu anlat\u0131rken was associated with demek, caused demekten neredeyse her zaman daha do\u011frudur. control fiilinin akademik kullan\u0131m\u0131 kontrol etmek de\u011fil de\u011fi\u015fkeni sabitlemektir: after controlling for income. T\xfcrk\xe7edeki kontrol etmek anlam\u0131 i\xe7in check kullan\u0131l\u0131r ve bu yalanc\u0131 e\u015f dost yaz\u0131\u015fmalarda da s\u0131k hata yarat\u0131r. theory de tahmin demek de\u011fildir: \u0130ngilizcede theory s\u0131nanm\u0131\u015f ve kabul g\xf6rm\xfc\u015f bir a\xe7\u0131klama \xe7er\xe7evesidir; T\xfcrk\xe7edeki teoride \xf6yle ama pratikte anlam\u0131n\u0131 vermek i\xe7in in principle ya da in theory kal\u0131b\u0131 kullan\u0131l\u0131r.")
B.bdi=s([B.b1r,B.aT1,B.aTV],t.q)
B.aCF=new A.p("The study tested three hypotheses about student motivation.","\xc7al\u0131\u015fma, \xf6\u011frenci motivasyonuna ili\u015fkin \xfc\xe7 hipotezi s\u0131nad\u0131.","hypothesis \xe7o\u011fulu hypotheses; test a hypothesis e\u015fdizimi",null)
B.az2=new A.p("The sample consisted of 240 undergraduates from two universities.","\xd6rneklem, iki \xfcniversiteden 240 lisans \xf6\u011frencisinden olu\u015ftu.","consist of; sample = \xf6rneklem, example de\u011fil",null)
B.awo=new A.p("The difference was statistically significant.","Fark istatistiksel olarak anlaml\u0131yd\u0131.","significant burada b\xfcy\xfckl\xfck de\u011fil istatistik bildirir",null)
B.aAr=new A.p("Income correlated positively with self-reported wellbeing, but the relationship was not causal.","Gelir, bildirilen iyi olma h\xe2liyle pozitif ili\u015fki g\xf6sterdi ancak ili\u015fki nedensel de\u011fildi.","correlate with; korelasyon nedensellik de\u011fildir",null)
B.at0=new A.p("Previous studies have shown that feedback improves accuracy; however, little attention has been paid to its timing.","\xd6nceki \xe7al\u0131\u015fmalar geri bildirimin do\u011frulu\u011fu art\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6stermi\u015ftir; ancak zamanlamas\u0131na az ilgi g\xf6sterilmi\u015ftir.","Literat\xfcr taramas\u0131n\u0131n iki klasik c\xfcmlesi: birikim + bo\u015fluk",null)
B.asW=new A.p("To date, few studies have examined this effect in bilingual learners.","Bug\xfcne kadar bu etkiyi iki dilli \xf6\u011frenenlerde inceleyen az say\u0131da \xe7al\u0131\u015fma yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.","Bo\u015fluk c\xfcmlesi: To date + few studies + present perfect",null)
B.aFx=new A.p("One limitation of the present study is its reliance on self-report data.","Bu \xe7al\u0131\u015fman\u0131n bir k\u0131s\u0131t\u0131, \xf6z bildirim verilerine dayanmas\u0131d\u0131r.","K\u0131s\u0131t\u0131 kendin adland\u0131r: limitation + reliance on",null)
B.auh=new A.p("These findings cannot be generalised to older learners.","Bu bulgular daha ileri ya\u015ftaki \xf6\u011frenenlere genellenemez.","generalise to: kapsam s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 a\xe7\u0131k\xe7a yaz",null)
B.bvA=s([B.aCF,B.az2,B.awo,B.aAr,B.at0,B.asW,B.aFx,B.auh],t.W)
B.aKZ=new A.O("Our results prove that the new method is better.","Our results indicate that the new method performs better under these conditions.","prove matematik d\u0131\u015f\u0131nda neredeyse kullan\u0131lmaz \xe7\xfcnk\xfc tek bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fma kan\u0131tlamaz; indicate, suggest ya da support ile birlikte ko\u015ful belirtmek akademik olarak do\u011fru olan bi\xe7imdir.",null)
B.aPv=new A.O("The improvement was very significant.","The improvement was substantial (12 per cent) and statistically significant.","significant akademik metinde istatistiksel anlaml\u0131l\u0131kt\u0131r ve very ile derecelendirilmez (\xe7ok k\xfc\xe7\xfck p de\u011ferleri i\xe7in highly significant denir, o da p de\u011feriyle birlikte); b\xfcy\xfckl\xfck i\xe7in substantial ya da considerable, \xf6l\xe7\xfc i\xe7in say\u0131 kullan\u0131l\u0131r.",null)
B.aLP=new A.O("The methodology we used was SPSS.","The data were analysed in SPSS; the study used a between-subjects design.","methodology y\xf6ntem se\xe7iminin gerek\xe7elendirildi\u011fi \xe7er\xe7evedir, bir yaz\u0131l\u0131m ya da ara\xe7 de\u011fil; ara\xe7 i\xe7in tool ya da software, i\u015flem i\xe7in method, ara\u015ft\u0131rma deseni i\xe7in design kullan\u0131l\u0131r.",null)
B.aKm=new A.O("This hypothesis was made by many researches.","This hypothesis has been proposed by a number of researchers.","research say\u0131lamayan bir isimdir, ara\u015ft\u0131rmac\u0131 ise researcher'd\u0131r; ayr\u0131ca hipotez make edilmez, propose ya da formulate edilir.",null)
B.b7b=s([B.aKZ,B.aPv,B.aLP,B.aKm],t.Z)
B.c6w=new A.bw("a-07-research-vocab","Ara\u015ft\u0131rma ve tez kelimeleri: y\xf6ntemden literat\xfcr taramas\u0131na","Bu ad\u0131mda tez, bildiri ve makale okuyup yazarken her g\xfcn ge\xe7en be\u015f y\xfcz ara\u015ft\u0131rma kelimesini \xf6\u011freniyorsun: hypothesis, methodology, sample size, variable, correlation, significant, reliability, limitation ve aileleri. Bu kelimelerin \xe7o\u011fu T\xfcrk\xe7ede de kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in tan\u0131d\u0131k gelir, ama \u0130ngilizcedeki teknik anlamlar\u0131 daha dard\u0131r: significant istatistiksel anlaml\u0131l\u0131k demektir, prove neredeyse hi\xe7 kullan\u0131lmaz, methodology ile method ayn\u0131 \u015fey de\u011fildir. \u0130kinci yar\u0131da literat\xfcr taramas\u0131n\u0131n sabit dilini \xe7al\u0131\u015facaks\u0131n: ne bilindi\u011fini, neyin eksik oldu\u011funu ve senin \xe7al\u0131\u015fman\u0131n o bo\u015flu\u011fu nas\u0131l kapatt\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yleyen \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmlelik kal\u0131p.",B.bdi,B.bvA,B.b7b,"Kelime tekrar\u0131 b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcnde ara\u015ft\u0131rma kelime paketini a\xe7 ve be\u015f y\xfcz kart\u0131 bitir; her kart\u0131n arkas\u0131na kelime ailesini (analyse / analysis / analytical) ve bir e\u015fdizimi yaz (test a hypothesis, draw a sample, control for a variable, draw a conclusion). Sonra kendi alan\u0131ndan bir makalenin giri\u015f b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcn\xfc oku ve \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmlelik bir literat\xfcr \xf6zeti sesli s\xf6yle: birinci c\xfcmle Previous studies have shown ile birikimi, ikinci c\xfcmle little attention has been paid ya da few studies have examined ile bo\u015flu\u011fu, \xfc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc c\xfcmle The present study addresses this gap by ile kendi konunu ba\u011flas\u0131n; metinde prove, very significant ve researches kelimelerini hi\xe7 kullanma.",B.M7,null,null,null,null)
B.aWW=new A.r("Be\u015f yuva ve uzunluk b\xfct\xe7esi","IMRAD mant\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131n s\u0131k\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015f h\xe2li be\u015f yuvad\u0131r: arka plan (bir iki c\xfcmle), ama\xe7 (bir c\xfcmle), y\xf6ntem (iki c\xfcmle), sonu\xe7lar (iki \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmle), \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m ve k\u0131s\u0131t (bir iki c\xfcmle). Arka plan c\xfcmlesi alan\u0131n ne bildi\u011fini ve neyin belirsiz kald\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 ayn\u0131 c\xfcmlede verir: Academic writing courses are widely offered, yet their effect on student performance remains unclear. Ama\xe7 c\xfcmlesi tek ve nettir: This study examines whether a four-week feedback intervention improves essay scores. Bu c\xfcmle yoksa okur makalenin sorusunu tahmin etmek zorunda kal\u0131r. Sonu\xe7lar yuvas\u0131 abstract'\u0131n merkezidir ve mutlaka say\u0131 i\xe7erir; sonucu s\xf6ylemeden sonu\xe7lar tart\u0131\u015f\u0131lacakt\u0131r demek en s\u0131k g\xf6r\xfclen ve en \xe7ok puan kaybettiren bo\u015fluktur. Kelime b\xfct\xe7esi dard\u0131r: 200 kelimede her c\xfcmle bir yuva doldurur. Ayn\u0131 yuvada iki c\xfcmle yazacaksan ba\u015fka bir yuvadan k\u0131smak zorundas\u0131n; bu y\xfczden abstract yazmak yazmaktan \xe7ok budamakt\u0131r.")
B.aRs=new A.r("Her yuvan\u0131n zaman\u0131 ve dili","Zaman se\xe7imi yuvaya g\xf6re de\u011fi\u015fir ve bu tutarl\u0131l\u0131k deneyimli yazar\u0131n imzas\u0131d\u0131r. Arka plan: geni\u015f zaman ve present perfect (remains unclear, has been widely studied). Ama\xe7: geni\u015f zaman ya da ge\xe7mi\u015f (This study examines / The aim of this study was to). Y\xf6ntem: ge\xe7mi\u015f zaman ve \xe7o\u011funlukla edilgen, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc kimin yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 de\u011fil neyin yap\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xf6nemlidir: Sixty first-year students were randomly assigned to two groups; Essays were scored by two trained raters. Sonu\xe7lar: ge\xe7mi\u015f zaman ve \xf6l\xe7\xfclebilir ifadeler: Scores improved by an average of 0.8 band points; No comparable change was observed in the control group. Olumsuz sonucu yazmak, olumlu sonucu yazmak kadar de\u011ferlidir. \xc7\u0131kar\u0131m: geni\u015f zaman ve hedge: These findings suggest that timing matters more than the volume of feedback. suggest ve may ikilisi tek bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fman\u0131n ta\u015f\u0131yabilece\u011fi iddia d\xfczeyidir. Son c\xfcmlede k\u0131s\u0131t bildirmek g\xfcveni art\u0131r\u0131r: The results should be interpreted with caution given the single-institution sample.")
B.aXZ=new A.r("Budama listesi: abstract'tan \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lacaklar","Abstract'tan ilk \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lacak \u015fey meta s\xf6ylemdir: In this paper, we will try to discuss\u2026 gibi c\xfcmleler yer kaplar ve hi\xe7bir bilgi vermez; onun yerine do\u011frudan This study examines\u2026 yaz\u0131l\u0131r. \u0130kinci \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lacak \u015fey g\xf6ndermelerdir: abstract tek ba\u015f\u0131na okundu\u011fu i\xe7in Figure 2, Section 4, as discussed below gibi ifadeler ve kural olarak at\u0131flar burada bulunmaz. \xdc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lacak \u015fey genel a\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015flard\u0131r: In today's world, technology is developing rapidly c\xfcmlesi okura hi\xe7bir \u015fey s\xf6ylemez ve kelime b\xfct\xe7esinin y\xfczde be\u015fini yer. D\xf6rd\xfcnc\xfcs\xfc tan\u0131ms\u0131z k\u0131saltmalard\u0131r: alan d\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan biri okuyacaksa k\u0131saltma ilk ge\xe7ti\u011fi yerde a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r ya da hi\xe7 kullan\u0131lmaz; ba\u015fl\u0131kta k\u0131saltma kullanmaktan da ka\xe7\u0131n\u0131l\u0131r. Son ad\u0131m anahtar kelimelerdir: ba\u015fl\u0131kta ge\xe7meyen ama aranacak \xfc\xe7 be\u015f terimi se\xe7, b\xf6ylece \xe7al\u0131\u015fman literat\xfcr taramalar\u0131nda bulunur. Ba\u015fl\u0131k da abstract'\u0131n par\xe7as\u0131 gibi \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r: m\xfcmk\xfcnse bulguyu ya da ili\u015fkiyi i\xe7erir.")
B.beY=s([B.aWW,B.aRs,B.aXZ],t.q)
B.axP=new A.p("Academic writing courses are widely offered, yet their effect on student performance remains unclear.","Akademik yazma dersleri yayg\u0131n bi\xe7imde veriliyor, ancak \xf6\u011frenci ba\u015far\u0131s\u0131 \xfczerindeki etkisi belirsiz kal\u0131yor.","Arka plan: ne biliniyor + ne belirsiz, tek c\xfcmlede",null)
B.aHB=new A.p("This study examines whether a four-week feedback intervention improves essay scores.","Bu \xe7al\u0131\u015fma, d\xf6rt haftal\u0131k bir geri bildirim m\xfcdahalesinin kompozisyon puanlar\u0131n\u0131 art\u0131r\u0131p art\u0131rmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 inceliyor.","Ama\xe7 yuvas\u0131: This study examines + whether",null)
B.ayx=new A.p("Sixty first-year students were randomly assigned to two groups.","Altm\u0131\u015f birinci s\u0131n\u0131f \xf6\u011frencisi rastgele bi\xe7imde iki gruba ayr\u0131ld\u0131.","Y\xf6ntem: ge\xe7mi\u015f zaman + edilgen",null)
B.aGa=new A.p("Essays were scored by two trained raters using an analytic rubric.","Kompozisyonlar, analitik bir dereceli puanlama anahtar\u0131yla iki e\u011fitimli puanlay\u0131c\u0131 taraf\u0131ndan de\u011ferlendirildi.","Y\xf6ntemin ikinci c\xfcmlesi: ara\xe7 ve puanlay\u0131c\u0131 say\u0131s\u0131",null)
B.aGl=new A.p("Scores improved by an average of 0.8 band points in the intervention group.","M\xfcdahale grubunda puanlar ortalama 0,8 bant puan\u0131 artt\u0131.","Sonu\xe7: by + ortalama; say\u0131 olmadan sonu\xe7 yaz\u0131lmaz",null)
B.aEX=new A.p("No comparable change was observed in the control group.","Kontrol grubunda benzer bir de\u011fi\u015fim g\xf6zlenmedi.","Olumsuz sonucu da yazmak sonucu yorumlanabilir k\u0131lar",null)
B.aw6=new A.p("These findings suggest that timing matters more than the volume of feedback.","Bu bulgular, zamanlaman\u0131n geri bildirimin miktar\u0131ndan daha \xf6nemli oldu\u011funu d\xfc\u015f\xfcnd\xfcr\xfcyor.","\xc7\u0131kar\u0131m: suggest ile \xf6l\xe7\xfcl\xfc genelleme",null)
B.aCq=new A.p("The results should be interpreted with caution given the single-institution sample.","\xd6rneklem tek bir kurumdan geldi\u011fi i\xe7in sonu\xe7lar dikkatle yorumlanmal\u0131d\u0131r.","K\u0131s\u0131t c\xfcmlesi g\xfcvenilirli\u011fi art\u0131r\u0131r",null)
B.bd_=s([B.axP,B.aHB,B.ayx,B.aGa,B.aGl,B.aEX,B.aw6,B.aCq],t.W)
B.aO2=new A.O("In this paper, we will try to discuss the important topic of feedback.","This study examines the effect of feedback timing on essay scores.","Abstract yap\u0131lacak i\u015fi de\u011fil yap\u0131lan i\u015fi anlat\u0131r; gelecek zaman ve try to kal\u0131b\u0131 hem belirsizdir hem de dar kelime b\xfct\xe7esini bo\u015fa harcar.",null)
B.aPj=new A.O("The results are shown in Figure 2 and discussed in Section 4.","Scores improved by 0.8 band points in the intervention group.","Abstract makaleden ayr\u0131 okunur; \u015fekil, tablo ve b\xf6l\xfcm g\xf6ndermeleri okura hi\xe7bir \u015fey s\xf6ylemez, onun yerine sonucun kendisi say\u0131yla yaz\u0131l\u0131r.",null)
B.aLD=new A.O("The aim of this study is to investigate feedback, and the results were very interesting.","The intervention group outperformed the control group by 12 per cent on the final essay.","Sonucu s\xf6ylemeden ilgin\xe7 demek bilgi ta\u015f\u0131maz; abstract'\u0131n merkez yuvas\u0131 \xf6l\xe7\xfclebilir bulgudur ve de\u011ferlendiriciler karar\u0131n\u0131 \xe7o\u011funlukla bu c\xfcmleye bakarak verir.",null)
B.aNP=new A.O("This study proves that feedback always improves writing.","These findings suggest that feedback may improve writing when it is provided early.","Tek bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fma kan\u0131tlamaz ve always gibi mutlak ifadeler ilk kar\u015f\u0131 \xf6rnekte \xe7\xf6ker; abstract'\u0131n \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m c\xfcmlesi suggest ve may d\xfczeyinde kal\u0131r.",null)
B.b7n=s([B.aO2,B.aPj,B.aLD,B.aNP],t.Z)
B.c6d=new A.bw("a-08-abstract-essay","Akademik \xf6zet (abstract): be\u015f yuva, iki y\xfcz kelime","Bu ad\u0131mda 150-250 kelimelik bir abstract yazmay\u0131 \xf6\u011freniyorsun: arka plan, ama\xe7, y\xf6ntem, sonu\xe7lar ve \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m yuvalar\u0131n\u0131 s\u0131rayla doldurmay\u0131. Abstract makalenin en \xe7ok okunan ve en az dikkatle yaz\u0131lan b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcd\xfcr; konferans de\u011ferlendiricileri ve okurlar\u0131n b\xfcy\xfck k\u0131sm\u0131 yaln\u0131zca bu metni okuyarak karar verir, dolay\u0131s\u0131yla tek ba\u015f\u0131na ayakta durmak zorundad\u0131r. T\xfcrk yazarlar\u0131n en s\u0131k hatas\u0131 abstract'\u0131 niyet beyan\u0131na \xe7evirmektir: ne yap\u0131laca\u011f\u0131 anlat\u0131l\u0131r, ne bulundu\u011fu s\xf6ylenmez. Bu ad\u0131mda her yuvan\u0131n kendi zaman\u0131n\u0131 ve kendi dilini \xf6\u011frenip sonucu say\u0131yla yazmay\u0131 al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131k h\xe2line getireceksin.",B.beY,B.bd_,B.b7n,"Essay b\xf6l\xfcm\xfcnde uzman seviyesinde \xfc\xe7 abstract yaz (her biri 150-250 kelime): biri kendi d\xf6nem ya da bitirme projenden, biri okudu\u011fun bir makaleyi kendi c\xfcmlelerinle \xf6zetleyen, biri hayali bir anket \xe7al\u0131\u015fmas\u0131ndan. Her metinde be\u015f yuva s\u0131rayla dolsun (arka plan, ama\xe7, y\xf6ntem, sonu\xe7lar, \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m ve k\u0131s\u0131t); ama\xe7 c\xfcmlesini This study examines ile, y\xf6ntem c\xfcmlelerini ge\xe7mi\u015f zaman ve edilgenle, sonu\xe7 c\xfcmlelerini en az iki say\u0131yla, \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m\u0131 suggest ya da may ile kur ve son c\xfcmlede bir k\u0131s\u0131t bildir. Hi\xe7birinde at\u0131f, \u015fekil ya da b\xf6l\xfcm g\xf6ndermesi, tan\u0131ms\u0131z k\u0131saltma ve In this paper we will try to \u2026 kal\u0131b\u0131 kullanma; her metnin alt\u0131na \xfc\xe7 anahtar kelime ekle.",B.j,null,null,null,null)
B.aXh=new A.r("Hedging: iddiay\u0131 kan\u0131t\u0131n b\xfcy\xfckl\xfc\u011f\xfcne g\xf6re ayarlamak","Hedging karars\u0131zl\u0131k de\u011fil hassasiyettir: elindeki kan\u0131t neyi ta\u015f\u0131yorsa onu s\xf6ylersin. Ara\xe7lar s\u0131n\u0131rl\u0131d\u0131r: kip fiilleri (may, might, could), fiiller (suggest, indicate, appear to, seem to, tend to), s\u0131fat ve zarflar (possible, likely, relatively, arguably, largely), niceleyiciler (most, in many cases, a majority of). Kritik kural \xfcst \xfcste bindirmemektir: It may possibly perhaps be somewhat true that\u2026 c\xfcmlesi yazar\u0131 karars\u0131z g\xf6sterir. Bir c\xfcmlede bir yumu\u015fat\u0131c\u0131 yeter; ikinci yumu\u015fat\u0131c\u0131 ancak farkl\u0131 bir boyutu s\u0131n\u0131rl\u0131yorsa eklenir. Kan\u0131t g\xfc\xe7l\xfcyse yumu\u015fatma da gereksizdir: clearly, demonstrably, the data leave little doubt ifadeleri nadiren ama yerinde kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda yaz\u0131ya g\xfc\xe7 katar; her c\xfcmlede kullan\u0131l\u0131rsa inand\u0131r\u0131c\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 bitirir. Hedging kapsam\u0131 da daralt\u0131r ve bu T\xfcrk \xf6\u011frencilerin en \xe7ok kazan\xe7 sa\u011flayaca\u011f\u0131 tekniktir: in this sample, under these conditions, in the Turkish context ifadeleri iddiay\u0131 savunulabilir k\u0131lar. Kar\u015f\u0131 u\xe7ta yer alan mutlak ifadeler (always, never, all researchers agree, it is impossible) tek bir kar\u015f\u0131 \xf6rnekle \xe7\xfcr\xfct\xfclebildi\u011fi i\xe7in akademik metinde neredeyse hi\xe7 kullan\u0131lmaz.")
B.aZs=new A.r("Nominalle\u015ftirme ile bilgi ak\u0131\u015f\u0131 ve isim y\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 tehlikesi","Nominalle\u015ftirme eylemi isme \xe7evirerek onu c\xfcmlenin \xf6znesi yapar: A control group was not used c\xfcmlesi The absence of a control group limits these conclusions h\xe2line geldi\u011finde ele\u015ftiri art\u0131k c\xfcmlenin merkezindedir. Bu teknik iki i\u015f yapar: bilinen bilgiyi c\xfcmle ba\u015f\u0131na alarak ak\u0131\u015f\u0131 kurar ve bir eylemi de\u011ferlendirilebilir bir nesne h\xe2line getirir (the failure of the model, the operationalisation of engagement, the exclusion of part-time students). Tehlikesi isim y\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131d\u0131r: The student writing performance improvement measurement procedure gibi zincirler okunmaz h\xe2le gelir \xe7\xfcnk\xfc hangi ismin hangisini niteledi\u011fi belirsizle\u015fir. Kural olarak \xfc\xe7ten fazla isim \xfcst \xfcste gelmemeli; gelmesi gerekiyorsa c\xfcmle of ve in edatlar\u0131yla ya da bir yan c\xfcmleyle a\xe7\u0131l\u0131r: It was unclear how improvements in student writing were measured. Yazd\u0131ktan sonra basit bir sa\u011flama yap: her c\xfcmlede eylemi ta\u015f\u0131yan bir fiil var m\u0131? C\xfcmlenin t\xfcm eylemi isimlere ta\u015f\u0131nd\u0131ysa ve fiil yaln\u0131zca is ya da has kald\u0131ysa c\xfcmleyi yeniden kur.")
B.aRw=new A.r("Ele\u015ftirel paragraf: iddia, kan\u0131t, de\u011ferlendirme, s\u0131n\u0131r","Ele\u015ftirel paragraf d\xf6rt katmanl\u0131d\u0131r: neyin tart\u0131\u015f\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yleyen iddia, kaynaktan gelen kan\u0131t, o kan\u0131t\u0131n ne kadar\u0131n\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131d\u0131\u011f\u0131n\u0131 s\xf6yleyen de\u011ferlendirme ve ge\xe7erlilik s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 \xe7izen son c\xfcmle. Betimleme ile de\u011ferlendirmeyi ay\u0131rmak \u015fartt\u0131r: The author used a questionnaire c\xfcmlesi betimlemedir; The questionnaire measured intention rather than behaviour, which weakens the causal claim c\xfcmlesi de\u011ferlendirmedir ve puan getiren k\u0131s\u0131m ikincisidir. De\u011ferlendirme y\xf6ntemin somut bir \xf6\u011fesine ba\u011flan\u0131r: \xf6rneklem se\xe7imi, \xf6l\xe7\xfcm arac\u0131, kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rma grubu, analiz birimi, d\u0131\u015flama \xf6l\xe7\xfctleri, kavram\u0131n i\u015fletimselle\u015ftirilmesi. Genel be\u011fenmedim ifadeleri ele\u015ftiri say\u0131lmaz. Kar\u015f\u0131 sav\u0131 \xf6d\xfcnle kar\u015f\u0131lamak en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc yap\u0131d\u0131r: While this explanation accounts for the 2008 data, it cannot explain the later divergence. B\xf6ylece kayna\u011f\u0131n hakl\u0131 oldu\u011fu yeri kabul eder, s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 g\xf6sterirsin. Son olarak korkuluk sav\u0131 (straw man) kurmaktan ka\xe7\u0131n: kar\u015f\u0131 g\xf6r\xfc\u015f\xfc en zay\u0131f h\xe2liyle \xf6zetleyip \xe7\xfcr\xfctmek, de\u011ferlendiricinin hemen fark etti\u011fi bir zay\u0131fl\u0131kt\u0131r; sav\u0131 en g\xfc\xe7l\xfc h\xe2liyle aktar\u0131p sonra s\u0131n\u0131rla.")
B.bzK=s([B.aXh,B.aZs,B.aRw],t.q)
