B.aRV=new A.r("\xdc\xe7 kay\u0131t seviyesi ve nerede kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131","\u0130ngilizcede selamla\u015fma \xfc\xe7 seviyede \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r: resm\xee (Good morning, it's a pleasure to meet you), n\xf6tr (Hello, nice to meet you) ve samimi (Hi, hey, good to see you). M\xfc\u015fteri, \xfcst y\xf6netim ve ilk tan\u0131\u015fma i\xe7in n\xf6tr seviye neredeyse her zaman en g\xfcvenli se\xe7imdir; resm\xee seviye yaz\u0131l\u0131 davetlerde ve protokol ortamlar\u0131nda kal\u0131r. Pleased to make your acquaintance gibi kal\u0131plar bug\xfcn sadece \xe7ok resm\xee yaz\u0131\u015fmalarda ge\xe7er, konu\u015furken kullan\u0131rsan eski kitaptan ezberlenmi\u015f gibi duyulur. \xc7o\u011fu uluslararas\u0131 \u015firkette ilk isimle hitap standartt\u0131r; kar\u015f\u0131 taraf kendini Elif diye tan\u0131tt\u0131ysa art\u0131k Ms. Demir demeye devam etmek mesafeyi yapay bi\xe7imde b\xfcy\xfct\xfcr. Kural basit: kar\u015f\u0131 taraf\u0131n se\xe7ti\u011fi seviyeyi bir ad\u0131m a\u015fmadan takip et, emin de\u011filsen bir t\u0131k daha resm\xee ba\u015fla ve onlar\u0131n a\xe7t\u0131\u011f\u0131 kadar samimile\u015f.")
B.aVA=new A.r("Tan\u0131\u015fma an\u0131n\u0131n sabit s\u0131ras\u0131","Tan\u0131\u015fma c\xfcmlesi neredeyse her zaman ayn\u0131 \xfc\xe7 par\xe7adan kurulur: selam, ad ve rol. Good morning, I'm Elif Demir from the finance team gibi. Rol\xfc s\xf6ylemek kibir de\u011fil, kar\u015f\u0131 tarafa hangi konuyu seninle konu\u015faca\u011f\u0131n\u0131 anlatan bir bilgidir; I lead the data team ya da I'm on the procurement side yeterlidir. Kar\u015f\u0131 taraf\u0131n ad\u0131n\u0131 duymad\u0131ysan sormak zorunludur: Sorry, could you say your name again? I want to get it right c\xfcmlesi nezaketsizlik de\u011fil, \xf6zen i\u015faretidir. Kendi ad\u0131n kar\u015f\u0131 taraf i\xe7in zorsa bir kez hecele ve bir kez telaffuz ver: It's Yasin, spelled Y-A-S-I-N, and it's pronounced ya-SEEN. Tan\u0131\u015fmadan sonra ismi bir kez daha kullanmak (Nice to meet you, Elif) hem kibar durur hem de ad\u0131 akl\u0131nda tutman\u0131 sa\u011flar.")
B.aSx=new A.r("Small talk ve konu\u015fmay\u0131 kapatmak","\u0130\u015f ortam\u0131nda small talk zaman kayb\u0131 de\u011fil, g\xfcven kurma ad\u0131m\u0131d\u0131r ve g\xfcvenli konular s\u0131n\u0131rl\u0131d\u0131r: yolculuk, mek\xe2n, etkinli\u011fin kendisi, g\xfcndemin yo\u011funlu\u011fu, hava. How was your flight? ya da Is this your first time in Istanbul? gibi sorular iki \xfc\xe7 c\xfcmle s\xfcrer, sonra g\xfcndeme ge\xe7ilir; maa\u015f, ya\u015f, medeni durum, din ve siyaset kapal\u0131d\u0131r. G\xfcndeme ge\xe7i\u015f bir c\xfcmleyle i\u015faretlenir: Thanks for making the time, shall we get started? Bu i\u015faret olmadan devam etmek kar\u015f\u0131 taraf\u0131 small talk'un ne zaman bitece\u011fi konusunda belirsiz b\u0131rak\u0131r. Kapan\u0131\u015f da ayn\u0131 \u015fekilde bir c\xfcmle ister ve mutlaka somut bir takip i\xe7erir: It was great meeting you, I'll send over the deck this afternoon. Daha \xf6nce tan\u0131\u015ft\u0131\u011f\u0131n biriyle nice to meet you demek en s\u0131k yap\u0131lan hatad\u0131r; ikinci kar\u015f\u0131la\u015fmadan sonras\u0131 her zaman nice to see you again'dir.")
B.bzQ=s([B.aRV,B.aVA,B.aSx],t.q)
