B.aSF=new A.r("A\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f: g\xf6zlem + soru + kendi pay\u0131n","\u0130yi bir a\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f \xfc\xe7 par\xe7adan olu\u015fur: ortak durumu adland\u0131ran bir g\xf6zlem, a\xe7\u0131k u\xe7lu k\u0131sa bir soru ve kendinden k\xfc\xe7\xfck bir bilgi. \xd6rne\u011fin bir etkinlikte This queue is unreal \u2014 have you been waiting long? I got here at eight c\xfcmlesi hem g\xf6zlem hem soru hem payd\u0131r. Sorunun a\xe7\u0131k u\xe7lu olmas\u0131 \u015fartt\u0131r: What brings you here? sorusu konu\u015fmay\u0131 a\xe7ar, Do you like it here? sorusu yes ile kapan\u0131r. G\xfcvenli a\xe7\u0131l\u0131\u015f konular\u0131 ortak durumdan \xe7\u0131kar: mek\xe2n, s\u0131ra, hava, yemek, m\xfczik, yolculuk, etkinli\u011fin kendisi. Kapal\u0131 konular ise maa\u015f, ya\u015f, kilo, din, siyaset ve ili\u015fki durumudur. C\xfcmleyi bir soruyla b\u0131rakma al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131\u011f\u0131 edin; soru olmadan verdi\u011fin bilgi kar\u015f\u0131 tarafa top vermeden yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015f bir a\xe7\u0131klama gibi kal\u0131r.")
B.aTO=new A.r("S\xfcrd\xfcrme: tepki, yank\u0131 sorusu, ekleme","Sohbeti s\xfcrd\xfcren \u015fey yeni sorular de\u011fil, verdi\u011fin tepkidir. Ana kal\u0131p \xfc\xe7 ad\u0131ml\u0131d\u0131r: k\u0131sa tepki, yank\u0131 sorusu, kendi benzer deneyimin. K\u0131sa tepkiler duyguya g\xf6re se\xe7ilir: Oh nice! ve That sounds great sevindirici habere, Oh no ve That's rough k\xf6t\xfc habere, Really? ve No way \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131c\u0131 habere gider. Yank\u0131 sorusu kar\u015f\u0131 taraf\u0131n son kelimesini tekrar eder: You moved from Lisbon? \u2014 For work, or...? Bu yap\u0131 yeni konu bulma y\xfck\xfcn\xfc s\u0131f\u0131ra indirir. Kendi pay\u0131n k\u0131sa olmal\u0131: iki c\xfcmle anlat, sonra topu geri ver (What about you?). \xdc\xe7 c\xfcmleyi ge\xe7en pay sohbeti monologa \xe7evirir. Sessizlik olursa panik yapma; Anyway, how do you know the host? gibi bir k\xf6pr\xfc c\xfcmlesi hem sessizli\u011fi kabul eder hem yeni konu a\xe7ar.")
B.aU3=new A.r("Kapan\u0131\u015f ve T\xfcrk\xe7e konu\u015fana \xf6zel k\xfclt\xfcrel notlar","Sohbeti ka\xe7arak bitirmek kabal\u0131k say\u0131l\u0131r; kapan\u0131\u015f \xfc\xe7 par\xe7al\u0131d\u0131r: sebep, iyi dilek, veda. I should go find my friend \u2014 it was great talking to you, enjoy the rest of your night. K\xfclt\xfcrel fark bir: How are you? \xe7o\u011fu durumda soru de\u011fil selamd\u0131r ve cevab\u0131 Good, thanks \u2014 you? kadard\u0131r; ger\xe7ek sa\u011fl\u0131k raporu vermek kar\u015f\u0131 taraf\u0131 \u015fa\u015f\u0131rt\u0131r. K\xfclt\xfcrel fark iki: \u0130ngilizce sosyal dilde do\u011frudanl\u0131k sertlik olarak okunur. T\xfcrk\xe7ede do\u011fal olan Neden geldin buraya? sorusunun kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 Why are you here? de\u011fil What brings you here? kal\u0131b\u0131d\u0131r. K\xfclt\xfcrel fark \xfc\xe7: Yak\u0131nl\u0131k dil bilgisiyle de\u011fil k\u0131saltma ve tonla kurulur. Contraction kullanmamak (I am, do not) c\xfcmleyi resm\xee ve mesafeli duyurur. K\xfclt\xfcrel fark d\xf6rt: Soru sorulmadan verilen ki\u015fisel bilgi (aile, gelir, hastal\u0131k) sosyal ortamda fazla payla\u015f\u0131m say\u0131l\u0131r; ilk sohbette y\xfczeyde kalmak yanl\u0131\u015f de\u011fil, beklenen davran\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.")
B.b9I=s([B.aSF,B.aTO,B.aU3],t.q)
