B.aRg=new A.c0("She go to work.","She goes to work.",'3. tekil \u015fah\u0131sta fiil sonuna -s/-es eklenir. "She/he/it" i\xe7in kural s\u0131k\u0131.',"With third-person singular subjects (he/she/it), the verb must take -s or -es. This rule has no exceptions.")
B.aNA=new A.c0("I no like coffee.","I don't like coffee.",'Olumsuzlama "no" ile de\u011fil "don\'t/doesn\'t" ile yap\u0131l\u0131r.',"Negatives are formed with don't/doesn't, not with \"no\" before the verb.")
B.aNo=new A.c0("Does she likes ice cream?","Does she like ice cream?",'Soru c\xfcmlesinde "does" zaten 3. tekil belirteci. Ana fiil yal\u0131n halde kal\u0131r.','"Does" already marks the third-person singular, so the main verb stays in its base form.')
B.b7z=s([B.aRg,B.aNA,B.aNo],t.gr)
B.cdF=new A.f8("Present Simple \u2014 Geni\u015f Zaman",'Genel do\u011frular, al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131klar ve tekrar eden eylemler. "Her g\xfcn", "genelde", "bazen" gibi s\u0131kl\u0131k zarflar\u0131yla beraber kullan\u0131l\u0131r.',"I/You/We/They + V1   \xb7   He/She/It + V1+s/es\nOlumsuz: don't/doesn't + V1   \xb7   Soru: Do/Does + \xf6zne + V1?","\u2022 Al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131klar: I drink coffee every morning.\n\u2022 Genel ger\xe7ekler: Water boils at 100\xb0C.\n\u2022 Tarifeli olaylar: The train leaves at 9 AM.\n\u2022 S\xfcrekli durumlar: She lives in Istanbul.",B.bdc,B.b7z,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "ben gelirim" derken hep yal\u0131n geliyor. \u0130ngilizcede 3. tekil \u015fah\u0131sta -s s\xfcrekli unutuluyor. \u015eu rutini kur: "He/She/It dedikten sonra fiilin ucuna mutlaka -s koyaca\u011f\u0131m."',"Present Simple","Used for general truths, habits, and repeated actions. Commonly paired with frequency adverbs such as always, usually, often, sometimes, and never.","\u2022 Habits: I drink coffee every morning.\n\u2022 General truths: Water boils at 100\xb0C.\n\u2022 Scheduled events: The train leaves at 9 AM.\n\u2022 Permanent states: She lives in Istanbul.","Turkish speakers often forget the third-person -s because Turkish has no equivalent ending. Build a habit: every time you use he/she/it, immediately add -s or -es to the verb.","I/You/We/They + V1   \xb7   He/She/It + V1+s/es\nNegative: don't/doesn't + V1   \xb7   Question: Do/Does + subject + V1?")
B.azD=new A.bo("I went to the cinema yesterday.","D\xfcn sinemaya gittim.","go \u2192 went","go \u2192 went (irregular)")
B.azw=new A.bo("She wrote a letter.","Bir mektup yazd\u0131.","write \u2192 wrote","write \u2192 wrote (irregular)")
B.aGB=new A.bo("They didn't come to the party.","Partiye gelmediler.",null,null)
B.awG=new A.bo("Did you see that movie?","O filmi g\xf6rd\xfcn m\xfc?",null,null)
B.b7R=s([B.azD,B.azw,B.aGB,B.awG],t.M6)
B.aQp=new A.c0("I goed to school.","I went to school.",'"go" d\xfczensiz bir fiildir; -ed eklenmez, "went" formunu al\u0131r. D\xfczensiz fiiller ezberlenir.','"Go" is an irregular verb \u2014 it does not take -ed. Its past form is "went", which must be memorised.')
B.aPa=new A.c0("She didn't went home.","She didn't go home.",'"didn\'t" zaten ge\xe7mi\u015f. Ana fiil V1 (yal\u0131n) kal\u0131r.','"Didn\'t" already marks the past tense, so the main verb returns to its base form.')
B.aJ5=new A.c0("Did you saw him?","Did you see him?",'"did" ge\xe7mi\u015f i\u015faretidir. Ana fiil yal\u0131n halde.','"Did" carries the past meaning, so the main verb must stay in its base form.')
B.buZ=s([B.aQp,B.aPa,B.aJ5],t.gr)
B.cdu=new A.f8("Past Simple \u2014 Di'li Ge\xe7mi\u015f",'Ge\xe7mi\u015fte ba\u015flay\u0131p biten olaylar. "D\xfcn", "ge\xe7en hafta", "2010\'da" gibi belirli zaman ifadeleriyle.',"Regular: V1 + ed (worked, played)\nIrregular: \xf6zel V2 formu (go \u2192 went, see \u2192 saw)\nOlumsuz: didn't + V1   \xb7   Soru: Did + \xf6zne + V1?","\u2022 Ge\xe7mi\u015fte biten olaylar: I visited Paris in 2019.\n\u2022 Ard\u0131\u015f\u0131k aksiyonlar: She woke up, made tea, and left.\n\u2022 Ge\xe7mi\u015fteki al\u0131\u015fkanl\u0131klar (used to alternatifi): I played football every weekend.",B.b7R,B.buZ,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "g\xf6rd\xfcm/yapt\u0131m/ko\u015ftum" hepsi d\xfczenli. \u0130ngilizcede ~200 d\xfczensiz fiil var. \xd6nce en s\u0131k 50\'sini ezberle (be/have/do/go/come/see/take/get...).',"Past Simple","Used for actions that started and finished in the past, typically with specific time markers such as yesterday, last week, or in 2010.","\u2022 Completed past events: I visited Paris in 2019.\n\u2022 Sequence of actions: She woke up, made tea, and left.\n\u2022 Past habits (alternative to used to): I played football every weekend.","Turkish speakers are accustomed to a fully regular past tense system. English has around 200 irregular verbs. Start by memorising the 50 most common ones: be, have, do, go, come, see, take, get, make, think\u2026","Regular: V1 + ed (worked, played)\nIrregular: special V2 form (go \u2192 went, see \u2192 saw)\nNegative: didn't + V1   \xb7   Question: Did + subject + V1?")
B.atd=new A.bo("I have lived in Ankara since 2018.","2018'den beri Ankara'da ya\u015f\u0131yorum.","h\xe2l\xe2 ya\u015f\u0131yor","still living there")
