B.cdA=new A.f8("Present Continuous \u2014 \u015eimdiki Zaman",'\u015eu anda devam eden veya ge\xe7ici olarak s\xfcren eylemler. "\u015eu an", "\u015fimdi", "bu hafta" gibi.',"am/is/are + V1+ing\nOlumsuz: am/is/are + not + V1+ing   \xb7   Soru: Am/Is/Are + \xf6zne + V1+ing?","\u2022 \u015eu an olan: I am studying English.\n\u2022 Ge\xe7ici durum: She is staying with us this week.\n\u2022 Planlanm\u0131\u015f yak\u0131n gelecek: We are meeting at 7 PM tonight.\n\u2022 De\u011fi\u015fen trend: The world is getting warmer.",B.bv0,B.b6p,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "biliyorum" \u015fimdiki zaman formunda. \u0130ngilizcede "I am knowing" YANLI\u015e. Stative (durum) fiillerin listesini \xf6\u011fren: know, like, love, hate, want, need, understand, believe...',"Present Continuous","Used for actions happening right now or temporary situations. Common with time expressions such as now, at the moment, this week, and today.","\u2022 Action happening now: I am studying English.\n\u2022 Temporary situation: She is staying with us this week.\n\u2022 Fixed future arrangement: We are meeting at 7 PM tonight.\n\u2022 Changing trend: The world is getting warmer.","Turkish speakers often try to use -ing with stative verbs because Turkish has no such restriction. Memorise the key stative verbs: know, like, love, hate, want, need, understand, believe, remember, prefer. These never take -ing in simple statements.","am/is/are + V1+ing\nNegative: am/is/are + not + V1+ing   \xb7   Question: Am/Is/Are + subject + V1+ing?")
B.aDl=new A.bo("I think it will be sunny tomorrow.","San\u0131r\u0131m yar\u0131n g\xfcne\u015fli olacak.","tahmin","prediction")
