B.aOm=new A.c0("I will study tonight. (\xf6nceden planlanm\u0131\u015f)","I'm going to study tonight.",'Plan yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015f \u2192 "going to". "Will" anl\u0131k karar i\xe7indir.','When a plan was decided in advance, use "going to". "Will" is reserved for spontaneous decisions made at the moment of speaking.')
B.aRa=new A.c0("She will to come.","She will come.",'"will" do\u011frudan V1 al\u0131r, "to" gerekmez.','"Will" is followed directly by the base verb, without "to".')
B.b50=s([B.aOm,B.aRa],t.gr)
B.cdD=new A.f8("Future: will vs going to","\u0130ngilizcede gelecek iki ayr\u0131 yap\u0131yla ifade edilir: anl\u0131k karar (will) ve \xf6nceden plan (going to). Aralar\u0131ndaki fark T\xfcrk\xe7ede yok.","will + V1   (anl\u0131k karar, tahmin, s\xf6z)\nam/is/are + going to + V1   (\xf6nceden plan, kan\u0131ta dayal\u0131 tahmin)","\u2022 Anl\u0131k karar: \"I'm thirsty.\" \u2014 \"I'll get you some water.\"\n\u2022 Tahmin/\xf6ng\xf6r\xfc: It will rain tomorrow.\n\u2022 S\xf6z/teklif: I'll help you with that.\n\u2022 \xd6nceden plan: I'm going to study medicine. (zaten karar verdim)\n\u2022 Kan\u0131ta dayal\u0131 tahmin: Look at the clouds \u2014 it's going to rain.",B.b73,B.b50,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "yapaca\u011f\u0131m" tek formdur. \u0130ngilizcede zihninde plan varsa "going to", o an karar veriyorsan "will" kullan. Bu fark\u0131 i\xe7selle\u015ftir.',"Future: will vs going to","English expresses the future in two distinct ways: will for spontaneous decisions or predictions, and going to for pre-made plans or evidence-based predictions. This distinction does not exist in Turkish.","\u2022 Spontaneous decision: \"I'm thirsty.\" \u2014 \"I'll get you some water.\"\n\u2022 General prediction: It will rain tomorrow.\n\u2022 Promise or offer: I'll help you with that.\n\u2022 Pre-made plan: I'm going to study medicine. (already decided)\n\u2022 Evidence-based prediction: Look at the clouds \u2014 it's going to rain.",'Turkish uses a single future form where English has two. The key question is: "Did I decide this before speaking?" If yes \u2192 going to. If the decision just popped into your head \u2192 will. Practise by narrating your daily plans aloud.',"will + V1   (instant decision, prediction, promise)\nam/is/are + going to + V1   (prior plan, evidence-based prediction)")
B.ayr=new A.bo("When we arrived, the movie had already started.","Biz vard\u0131\u011f\u0131m\u0131zda film \xe7oktan ba\u015flam\u0131\u015ft\u0131.",null,null)
