B.aOn=new A.c0("When I came home, my brother was eaten dinner.","When I came home, my brother had eaten dinner.","\u0130ki ge\xe7mi\u015f olayda \xf6nce olan: had + V3.","When two past actions are mentioned, the one that occurred first takes had + V3 (past perfect).")
B.bbc=s([B.aOn],t.gr)
B.cdy=new A.f8("Past Perfect \u2014 Ge\xe7mi\u015ften \xd6nceki Ge\xe7mi\u015f",'Ge\xe7mi\u015fteki bir noktadan \xd6NCE olmu\u015f eylemler. "...etmi\u015fti" \u2014 T\xfcrk\xe7edeki "mi\u015f\'li ge\xe7mi\u015f" gibi.',"had + V3 (past participle)\nOlumsuz: hadn't + V3   \xb7   Soru: Had + \xf6zne + V3?","\u2022 \u0130ki ge\xe7mi\u015f eylem var, hangisi \xf6nce: When I arrived, the train had left.\n\u2022 Reported speech'te tense backshift.\n\u2022 3rd conditional: If I had known...",B.buo,B.bbc,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "yemi\u015fti" \u2192 had eaten. "\u0130ki olay var, hangisi daha \xf6nce?" sorusunu sor. \xd6nce olan past perfect, sonra olan past simple.',"Past Perfect","Used for an action that happened before another point or action in the past. It establishes a clear time sequence between two past events.","\u2022 Two past events, the earlier one: When I arrived, the train had left.\n\u2022 Tense backshift in reported speech.\n\u2022 Third conditional: If I had known\u2026",'Ask yourself: "Which of the two past events happened first?" The earlier one uses past perfect (had + V3), the later one uses past simple. Turkish speakers sometimes skip past perfect since Turkish handles sequence differently \u2014 but in English, clarity about time order is essential.',"had + V3 (past participle)\nNegative: hadn't + V3   \xb7   Question: Had + subject + V3?")
