B.aJQ=new A.c0("I live in the Turkey.","I live in Turkey.","\xc7o\u011fu \xfclke ismi artikelsizdir. \u0130stisnalar: the USA, the UK, the Netherlands (\xe7o\u011ful/birle\u015fik).","Most country names take no article. Exceptions include the USA, the UK, and the Netherlands \u2014 names that are plural or compound.")
B.aPq=new A.c0("I want to be a engineer.","I want to be an engineer.","engineer \xfcnl\xfc SESLE ba\u015fl\u0131yor \u2192 an. Kural harfe de\u011fil sese bakar.",'"Engineer" starts with a vowel sound, so "an" is required.')
B.bs0=s([B.aQ_,B.aP6,B.aJQ,B.aPq],t.gr)
B.cdj=new A.f8("Artikeller: a / an / the","T\xfcrk\xe7ede artikel YOK. Bu y\xfczden T\xfcrklerin en s\u0131k kar\u0131\u015ft\u0131rd\u0131\u011f\u0131 yap\u0131. Belirli (the) ve belirsiz (a/an) ayr\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 mant\u0131kla yap.",'a + \xfcns\xfcz SESLE ba\u015flayan tekil isim (a book, a university)\nan + \xfcnl\xfc SESLE ba\u015flayan tekil isim (an apple, an hour)\n\u26a0 Yaz\u0131ma de\u011fil SESE bak: university "yu" diye ba\u015flar \u2192 a; hour\'da h okunmaz \u2192 an.\nthe + belirli, daha \xf6nce bahsedilen, tek olan (the sun, the book I bought)',"\u2022 \u0130lk bahis (yeni): I saw a dog. (herhangi bir k\xf6pek)\n\u2022 Tekrar bahis: The dog was huge. (az \xf6nceki k\xf6pek)\n\u2022 Tek olan: the sun, the moon, the President\n\u2022 S\xfcperlatif: the best, the most\n\u2022 Genelleme \u2014 artikel yok: I like cats. (kediler genel olarak)\n\u2022 \u015eehir/\xfclke (genelde): I live in Turkey. (artikelsiz)\n\u2022 Nehirler/denizler: the Nile, the Black Sea (the'l\u0131)",B.brX,B.bs0,"Zihinsel checklist: (1) Tekil say\u0131labilir isim mi? (2) \u0130lk bahis mi? \u2192 a/an. (3) Belirli/daha \xf6nce ge\xe7ti mi? \u2192 the. (4) Genel mi? \u2192 artikel yok. Bu s\u0131ralamay\u0131 her isim \xf6ncesi \xe7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.","Articles: a / an / the","Turkish has no articles, making this one of the most common stumbling blocks for Turkish learners. The key is understanding the distinction between definite (the) and indefinite (a/an).","\u2022 First mention (new noun): I saw a dog. (any dog)\n\u2022 Second mention (known noun): The dog was huge. (the one just mentioned)\n\u2022 Unique referents: the sun, the moon, the President\n\u2022 Superlatives: the best, the most\n\u2022 Generalisations \u2014 no article: I like cats. (cats in general)\n\u2022 Cities/countries (usually): I live in Turkey. (no article)\n\u2022 Rivers/seas: the Nile, the Black Sea (with the)","Turkish speakers tend to omit articles entirely or add them randomly. Run this mental checklist before every noun: (1) Is it singular and countable? (2) First mention? \u2192 a/an. (3) Specific or already known? \u2192 the. (4) General? \u2192 no article. With practice this becomes automatic.",'a + singular noun starting with a consonant sound (a book, a university)\nan + singular noun starting with a vowel sound (an apple, an hour)\n\u26a0 Go by the sound, not the spelling: university starts with a "yoo" sound \u2192 a; the h in hour is silent \u2192 an.\nthe + specific, already mentioned, one of a kind (the sun, the book I bought)')
