B.cdE=new A.f8("Edatlar: in / on / at","Yer ve zaman edatlar\u0131 b\xfcy\xfck \xf6l\xe7\xfcde kal\u0131pla\u015fm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. Mant\u0131kla de\u011fil, kal\u0131p olarak \xf6\u011frenilir.","Yer: in (i\xe7inde, b\xfcy\xfck) \xb7 on (\xfcst\xfcnde, y\xfczeyde) \xb7 at (noktada, adres)\nZaman: in (ay/y\u0131l) \xb7 on (g\xfcn/tarih) \xb7 at (saat/an)","\u2022 at: at the station, at 5 PM, at the door (nokta)\n\u2022 on: on the table, on Monday, on the bus (y\xfczey/g\xfcn)\n\u2022 in: in the box, in May, in 2024, in the morning (i\xe7inde)",B.bcS,B.bco,"En s\u0131k 30 kal\u0131b\u0131 ezberle: at home, at school, at work, at night, in the morning, in the evening, on Monday, on time, in time, on TV, in the news... S\xf6zl\xfckten de\u011fil, c\xfcmle i\xe7inde \xf6\u011fren.","Prepositions: in / on / at","Prepositions of place and time are largely fixed collocations. They are best learnt as set phrases rather than through logical rules alone.","\u2022 at: at the station, at 5 PM, at the door (a point or specific location)\n\u2022 on: on the table, on Monday, on the bus (a surface or a day)\n\u2022 in: in the box, in May, in 2024, in the morning (inside or a period)","Turkish speakers often translate the Turkish locative suffix (-da/-de) directly, which leads to inconsistent choices. Instead, memorise the 30 most frequent collocations as fixed phrases: at home, at school, at work, at night, in the morning, on Monday, on time, on TV\u2026","Place: in (inside, large areas) \xb7 on (on a surface) \xb7 at (a point, an address)\nTime: in (month/year) \xb7 on (day/date) \xb7 at (clock time/moment)")
B.aGo=new A.bo("You should drink more water.","Daha fazla su i\xe7melisin.","tavsiye","advice")
B.asL=new A.bo("She must be at home now.","\u015eimdi evde olmal\u0131.","g\xfc\xe7l\xfc tahmin","strong deduction")
B.aCh=new A.bo("Can you help me?","Bana yard\u0131m edebilir misin?",null,null)
