B.aQ0=new A.c0("The window broke by him.","The window was broken by him.",'Edilgen yap\u0131 "to be + V3" ister. "broke" V2; "broken" V3.','The passive requires "to be + past participle (V3)". "Broke" is the simple past (V2); the correct participle is "broken".')
B.bfT=s([B.aQ0],t.gr)
B.cdx=new A.f8("Edilgen Yap\u0131 (Passive Voice)","Eylemin kim taraf\u0131ndan yap\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131 \xf6nemli olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda veya nesne \xf6ne \xe7\u0131kar\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda. Akademik yaz\u0131da \xe7ok yayg\u0131n.","to be + V3 (past participle)\nEtken: Subject + V + Object   \u2192   Edilgen: Object + to be + V3 (+ by Agent)","\u2022 Kim yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131 belirsiz: My wallet was stolen.\n\u2022 Akademik objektiflik: The experiment was conducted.\n\u2022 S\xfcre\xe7 anlat\u0131m\u0131: Coffee beans are grown in Brazil.",B.bs2,B.bfT,'T\xfcrk\xe7edeki "-\u0131ld\u0131, -ildi, -uldu" edilgen ekleri direkt kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131d\u0131r. "Yap\u0131ld\u0131" \u2192 was done. "Yaz\u0131l\u0131r" \u2192 is written.',"Passive Voice","Used when the doer of an action is unknown, unimportant, or deliberately omitted. Very common in academic writing and formal contexts.","\u2022 Unknown doer: My wallet was stolen.\n\u2022 Academic objectivity: The experiment was conducted.\n\u2022 Process description: Coffee beans are grown in Brazil.","Turkish speakers usually grasp the concept of passive quickly because Turkish has clear passive suffixes (-\u0131l/-il/-ul/-\xfcl). The challenge is remembering to use the correct past participle (V3) rather than the simple past (V2). Always check: be + V3, never be + V2.","Active: Subject + V + Object   \u2192   Passive: Object + to be + V3 (+ by Agent)")
B.aBA=new A.bo("He said he had finished his homework.","\xd6devini bitirdi\u011fini s\xf6yledi.","have \u2192 had","backshift: have finished \u2192 had finished")
