B.aJe=new A.c0("He said that he is happy.","He said that he was happy.","Said (past) \u2192 i\xe7erideki tense bir ad\u0131m geri (is \u2192 was).","When the reporting verb is in the past (said), the reported verb must shift back: is \u2192 was.")
B.bbZ=s([B.aJe],t.gr)
B.cdv=new A.f8("Dolayl\u0131 Anlat\u0131m (Reported Speech)",'Ba\u015fkas\u0131n\u0131n s\xf6yledi\u011fini aktarmak. "Tense backshift" kural\u0131: ana c\xfcmle past ise i\xe7erideki tense bir ad\u0131m geriye gider.',"said that + tense backshift\npresent \u2192 past   \xb7   past \u2192 past perfect   \xb7   will \u2192 would   \xb7   can \u2192 could",'\u2022 Do\u011frudan: He said, "I am tired."\n\u2022 Dolayl\u0131: He said (that) he was tired.\n\u2022 Do\u011frudan: She said, "I will come."\n\u2022 Dolayl\u0131: She said (that) she would come.',B.bt8,B.bbZ,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "dedi ki \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yorum" \u2192 "dedi ki \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yordu" \u015feklinde de\u011fi\u015fmez. \u0130ngilizcede backshift zorunlu. \u015eu kal\u0131b\u0131 ezberle: said (past) \u2192 bir ad\u0131m geri.',"Reported Speech","Used to report what someone else said. The key rule is tense backshift: when the reporting verb is in the past, the reported verb shifts one tense back in time.",'\u2022 Direct: He said, "I am tired."\n\u2022 Reported: He said (that) he was tired.\n\u2022 Direct: She said, "I will come."\n\u2022 Reported: She said (that) she would come.',"Turkish speakers often keep the original tense inside reported speech because Turkish does not require backshift. In English, backshift is mandatory when the reporting verb is past. Memorise the chain: is \u2192 was, will \u2192 would, can \u2192 could, have \u2192 had.",null)
