B.bzu=s([B.aKv],t.gr)
B.cdI=new A.f8("\xd6zne-Y\xfcklem Uyumu",'\xd6zne tekilse fiil tekil (he plays), \xe7o\u011fulsa \xe7o\u011ful (they play). "Each", "everyone", "neither" tekil saymak gibi tuzaklara dikkat.',"Tekil \xf6zne \u2192 -s'li fiil (3. tekil)\n\xc7o\u011ful \xf6zne \u2192 yal\u0131n fiil\nTuzaklar: everyone/each/neither (tekil) \xb7 police/people (\xe7o\u011ful)","\u2022 My friend likes pizza. (tekil)\n\u2022 My friends like pizza. (\xe7o\u011ful)\n\u2022 Everyone is here. (everyone tekil say\u0131l\u0131r)\n\u2022 The police are investigating. (police \xe7o\u011ful)",B.bhW,B.bzu,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "herkes geldiler" denmez ama "geldiler" \xe7o\u011ful. \u0130ngilizcede "everyone is/comes" tekil. Bu fark\u0131 hat\u0131rla.',"Subject\u2013Verb Agreement","A singular subject takes a singular verb, and a plural subject takes a plural verb. Watch out for tricky words like each, everyone, and neither, which are grammatically singular.","\u2022 My friend likes pizza. (singular)\n\u2022 My friends like pizza. (plural)\n\u2022 Everyone is here. (everyone = singular)\n\u2022 The police are investigating. (police = always plural)",'Turkish speakers sometimes say "everyone are" by analogy with a plural group. In English, every-, some-, and no- compounds (everyone, somebody, nothing) are always singular. Also remember that "each" and "either/neither" trigger singular verbs even when followed by "of the students".',"Singular subject \u2192 verb + -s (3rd person singular)\nPlural subject \u2192 base verb\nTraps: everyone/each/neither (singular) \xb7 police/people (plural)")
