B.aMJ=new A.c0("She is more taller than me.","She is taller than me.",'"more" ve "-er" ayn\u0131 anda kullan\u0131lmaz.','You cannot use "more" and "-er" at the same time. Choose one based on the number of syllables.')
B.aK4=new A.c0("It is the most best.","It is the best.",'"best" zaten en \xfcst d\xfczey; "most" eklenmez.','"Best" is already a superlative. Adding "most" creates a redundant double superlative.')
B.buP=s([B.aMJ,B.aK4],t.gr)
B.cdC=new A.f8("Kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rma: more/-er, the most/-est","K\u0131sa s\u0131fatlar -er/-est al\u0131r (big \u2192 bigger \u2192 the biggest). Uzun s\u0131fatlar more/most al\u0131r (beautiful \u2192 more beautiful \u2192 the most beautiful).","1 hece: -er/-est (tall \u2192 taller)\n2 hece -y biten: -ier/-iest (happy \u2192 happier)\n3+ hece: more/most (interesting \u2192 more interesting)\n\u0130stisnalar: good \u2192 better \u2192 best, bad \u2192 worse \u2192 worst","\u0130ki ki\u015fi/\u015fey kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rma: -er + than. \xdc\xe7l\xfc+ \xfcst d\xfczey: the + -est / the most.",B.b98,B.buP,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "daha g\xfczel" hepsi ayn\u0131. \u0130ngilizcede hece say\u0131s\u0131na bak: 1 hece \u2192 -er, 3+ hece \u2192 more. 2 hece s\u0131n\u0131rda; s\xf6zl\xfc\u011fe g\xfcven.',"Comparatives and Superlatives","Short adjectives form comparatives and superlatives with -er/-est. Long adjectives use more/most. Irregular forms such as good \u2192 better \u2192 best must be memorised.","Comparing two things: -er + than. Ranking three or more: the + -est / the most.",'Turkish uses "daha" (more) for all comparatives regardless of syllable count. English requires you to choose: one syllable \u2192 -er (taller); three or more syllables \u2192 more (more interesting). Two-syllable adjectives vary \u2014 when in doubt, consult a dictionary or use "more" as the safe default.',"1 syllable: -er/-est (tall \u2192 taller)\n2 syllables ending in -y: -ier/-iest (happy \u2192 happier)\n3+ syllables: more/most (interesting \u2192 more interesting)\nExceptions: good \u2192 better \u2192 best, bad \u2192 worse \u2192 worst")
