B.aBW=new A.bo("You must be exhausted after that flight.","O u\xe7u\u015ftan sonra bitkin olmal\u0131s\u0131n.","kan\u0131ta dayal\u0131 g\xfc\xe7l\xfc tahmin","strong guess based on evidence")
B.aDD=new A.bo("She might still be at the office.","H\xe2l\xe2 ofiste olabilir.","ihtimal \u2014 emin de\u011filsin","possibility \u2014 you are not sure")
B.aIO=new A.bo("That can't be her car; hers is blue.","O onun arabas\u0131 olamaz; onunki mavi.","olumsuz \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m \u2192 can't","negative deduction takes can't")
B.aAd=new A.bo("He must have forgotten the meeting.","Toplant\u0131y\u0131 unutmu\u015f olmal\u0131.","ge\xe7mi\u015f \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m \u2192 must have + V3","past deduction \u2192 must have + V3")
B.avi=new A.bo("They could have missed the train.","Treni ka\xe7\u0131rm\u0131\u015f olabilirler.","ge\xe7mi\u015f i\xe7in zay\u0131f tahmin","weak guess about the past")
B.b9u=s([B.aBW,B.aDD,B.aIO,B.aAd,B.avi],t.M6)
B.aMf=new A.c0("She mustn't be at home, her car is gone.","She can't be at home, her car is gone.",'"mustn\'t" yasak bildirir ("yapmamal\u0131s\u0131n"), tahmin de\u011fil. Olumsuz \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m her zaman "can\'t" ile kurulur.','"Mustn\'t" expresses prohibition, not deduction. A negative deduction is always formed with "can\'t" in the present, or "couldn\'t have" in the past.')
B.aNg=new A.c0("I think she can be at work.","She might be at work.",'T\xfcrk\xe7e "olabilir" birebir "can be" diye \xe7evrilince bozuluyor: "can" yetenek ve genel ihtimal anlat\u0131r. Belirli bir durum hakk\u0131ndaki tahmin might / may / could ister.','Turkish "olabilir" translates word for word as "can be", but "can" expresses ability or general possibility. For a guess about one specific situation, use might, may or could.')
B.aLX=new A.c0("It must rain last night; the ground is wet.","It must have rained last night; the ground is wet.","Ge\xe7mi\u015f hakk\u0131nda tahmin y\xfcr\xfct\xfcrken modalin kendisi ge\xe7mi\u015fe \xe7ekilmez, ondan sonras\u0131 \xe7ekilir: must + have + V3.","When you speculate about the past, the modal itself never changes form; what follows it does: must + have + V3.")
B.aLx=new A.c0("He must have went home.","He must have gone home.",'"have" zinciri hep \xfc\xe7\xfcnc\xfc h\xe2li ister. "went" ikinci h\xe2l; burada do\u011fru bi\xe7im "gone".','After "have" you always need the third form of the verb. "Went" is the past simple form; the correct one here is "gone".')
B.bpS=s([B.aMf,B.aNg,B.aLX,B.aLx],t.gr)
B.cdt=new A.f8("\xc7\u0131kar\u0131m Modallar\u0131 \u2014 must / might / can't","Emin olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131n bir \u015fey hakk\u0131nda tahmin y\xfcr\xfctmenin yolu. Ne kadar emin oldu\u011funu c\xfcmledeki modal s\xf6yler: must (neredeyse eminim), might/could (olabilir), can't (imk\xe2ns\u0131z). Zorunluluk anlatm\u0131yorsun, kan\u0131ttan sonu\xe7 \xe7\u0131kar\u0131yorsun.","\u015e\u0130MD\u0130:   must / might / may / could / can't + V1\nGE\xc7M\u0130\u015e:  must / might / may / could / can't + have + V3\nOlumsuz \xe7\u0131kar\u0131m \"mustn't\" ile DE\u011e\u0130L, \"can't / couldn't\" ile kurulur.","\u2022 G\xfc\xe7l\xfc tahmin (kan\u0131t var): You must be tired.\n\u2022 Zay\u0131f tahmin (ihtimal): She might be in a meeting.\n\u2022 Eledi\u011fin ihtimal: That can't be his brother.\n\u2022 Ge\xe7mi\u015f hakk\u0131nda tahmin: They must have left early.\n\u2022 Kibarl\u0131k arac\u0131 olarak: You must be exhausted after that flight.",B.b9u,B.bpS,'T\xfcrk\xe7ede "-meli/-mal\u0131" iki i\u015fi birden g\xf6r\xfcyor: "gitmelisin" zorunluluk, "yorgun olmal\u0131s\u0131n" tahmin. \u0130ngilizcede bunlar ayr\u0131l\u0131r ve as\u0131l tuzak olumsuzda: tahminin olumsuzu "mustn\'t" de\u011fil "can\'t"tir. K\u0131sa kural: neredeyse eminsen must, emin de\u011filsen might, eliyorsan can\'t.',"Modals of Deduction \u2014 must / might / can't","This is how you work out what is probably true when you do not know for certain. The modal itself carries your level of confidence: must (almost certain), might or could (possible), can't (ruled out). You are not expressing obligation here, you are reading the evidence.","\u2022 Strong guess with evidence: You must be tired.\n\u2022 Weak guess: She might be in a meeting.\n\u2022 Something you rule out: That can't be his brother.\n\u2022 Guessing about the past: They must have left early.\n\u2022 As a politeness move: You must be exhausted after that flight.","A single Turkish suffix carries both obligation and deduction, so the two blur together in English. Keep them apart with one short rule: almost certain gives you must, possible gives you might, ruled out gives you can't. The trap is the negative: the opposite of a deduction is never \"mustn't\", which tells someone not to do something.","NOW:     must / might / may / could / can't + V1\nPAST:    must / might / may / could / can't + have + V3\nA negative deduction uses NOT \"mustn't\" but \"can't / couldn't\".")
B.c_H=new A.Z(B.caZ,[B.cdt],t.mp)
